        <bpmn:serviceTask id="C_stamp" name="Stamp entries for goals that supply their own&#10;curation — step 0">
          <bpmn:documentation>workflows/learn/skills/curation/SKILL.md, step 0. A goal whose supply slot names anything but `curated` produces its own activities — a vocabulary word&#39;s moves come from the six-move menu, not from this file — so there is no artifact to find and no menu to choose among. What it needs is one entry carrying `origin: generated`, so that every goal is reachable through the same lookup and review never has to ask what kind of goal it is looking at. Idempotent, and outside the revision loop: it runs once per curation run, and a goal that already has its entry is left alone.</bpmn:documentation>
